    "answer": {
      "short": "Mary is right. Both inequalities give $-3\\le x\\le-1$; the original restriction $x\\ne2$ removes no value from this interval.",
      "worked": "The original denominator requires $x\\ne2$. For these values,\n$$\\left|\\frac{(x-2)(x+2)}{x-2}\\right|=|x+2|.$$\n$$\\begin{align*}-1&\\le x+2\\le1\\\\-3&\\le x\\le-1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe excluded value $2$ is outside this interval, so the original and simplified inequalities have the same solution. Mary is right.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
